{"data":{"status":true,"competition":{"id":1767342,"visibility":"public","theme_colour":null,"paid":0,"title":"Worst UI","festival_id":null,"organization_id":627,"web_url":null,"start_date":"2026-10-07T00:00:00+05:30","end_date":"2026-10-15T00:00:00+05:30","location":null,"type":"competitions","public_url":"competitions\/worst-ui-indraprastha-institute-of-information-technology-iiit-delhi-1767342","region":"offline","details":"<p><strong>Eligibility:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>The competition is open to <strong>college\/university students only<\/strong>.<\/li>\n<li>Students from any college, university, branch, or specialization are eligible.<\/li>\n<li>This is an <strong>individual competition<\/strong>; participants must compete independently.<\/li>\n<li><strong>Inter-specialization participation is allowed<\/strong>, as there are no restrictions based on academic branch or specialization.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Format:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>The competition will consist of <strong>3&ndash;4 rounds<\/strong>.<\/li>\n<li>Each round will be independent, and participants can choose to participate in any round they feel is feasible for them.<\/li>\n<li>In each round, participants will be given a specific UI\/interface or component to design.<\/li>\n<li>Participants will be given a <strong>fixed time limit for each round<\/strong> to design their interface.<\/li>\n<li>The problem statement and time limit for each round will be announced at the beginning of the respective round.<\/li>\n<li>At the end of each round, participants will submit\/present their designs for evaluation.<\/li>\n<li>A winner will be selected for each round.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Rules:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>Participants must compete <strong>individually<\/strong>. No teams or collaboration between participants are allowed.<\/li>\n<li>The objective is to intentionally create the <strong>worst possible\/most irritating user interface<\/strong> for the given problem statement while keeping it functional.<\/li>\n<li>Designs should be confusing, inconvenient, unintuitive, unnecessarily complex, or creatively frustrating.<\/li>\n<li>Participants must work on the problem statement assigned for the respective round.<\/li>\n<li>All designs must be created and submitted within the allotted time.<\/li>\n<li>Designs must be original and created by the participant during the competition.<\/li>\n<li>Plagiarism, copying another participant's work, or collaborating with another participant will result in disqualification.<\/li>\n<li>Judging will be based on <strong>worst usability, creativity, unnecessary complexity, confusing user experience, and entertainment value<\/strong>.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Judging Criteria:<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><strong>Each submission will be evaluated on:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Worst Usability<\/strong> &ndash; How difficult and frustrating the interface is to use.<\/li>\n<li><strong>Creativity<\/strong> &ndash; How creatively the participant makes the interface bad.<\/li>\n<li><strong>Unnecessary Complexity<\/strong> &ndash; The extent of needless complexity introduced.<\/li>\n<li><strong>Confusing UX<\/strong> &ndash; How unintuitive and confusing the interface is.<\/li>\n<li><strong>Entertainment Value<\/strong> &ndash; How humorous and entertaining the design is.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><strong>Winner &amp; Rewards:<\/strong><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>A winner will be selected for each round.<\/li>\n<li>Winners will receive rewards\/prizes as decided by the organizing team.<\/li>\n<\/ul>","overall_prizes":null,"regn_open":1,"regn_type":1,"regn_url":null,"regn_email":"","registration_clicks":0,"user_id":4335091,"moderation_status":1,"overall_leaderboard":0,"reject_reason":null,"display_date":null,"created_at":"2026-10-07T17:38:08+05:30","updated_at":"2026-10-07T18:14:02+05:30","communication_sent":null,"certificate_at":null,"remarks":null,"branding":0,"disable_auto_rounds":null,"certificate_config":null,"subtype":"general_competitio